<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cape Passaro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1718">1718</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-quadruple-alliance">War of the Quadruple Alliance</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cape Passaro was fought on 11 August 1718 off the south-eastern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, where a British fleet under Admiral Sir George Byng destroyed a Spanish fleet supporting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s invasion of Sicily. Although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and Spain were not yet formally at war, the battle crippled the Spanish navy and helped force Spain to abandon its attempt to recover its former Italian lands.</p></div>
